STAAD SPACE
START JOB INFORMATION
ENGINEER DATE 24-Nov-26
JOB NAME STAAD ROUND 4 PROBE
END JOB INFORMATION
INPUT WIDTH 79
* ---- Pluto's STAAD round 4 probe (scripts/lib/probes/README.md): units changing along the file under every kind of
* ---- number, load envelopes, and a code check per load case. Run it as it is, and Pluto's copy of it.
UNIT FEET KIP
JOINT COORDINATES
1 0 0 0; 2 0 12 0; 3 20 12 0; 4 20 0 0; 5 0 12 15; 6 20 12 15;
7 0 0 15; 8 20 0 15; 9 10 12 0; 11 10 12 15;
MEMBER INCIDENCES
1 1 2; 2 7 5; 3 4 3; 4 8 6; 5 2 9; 6 9 3; 7 5 11; 8 2 5; 9 3 6; 10 9 11;
11 11 6;
ELEMENT INCIDENCES SHELL
101 2 9 11 5;
START GROUP DEFINITION
MEMBER
_COLUMNS 1 TO 4
GEOMETRY
_BEAMS 5 TO 9 11
FLOOR
_ROOF 5 6 7 11
END GROUP DEFINITION
* materials in kN and mm
UNIT MMS KN
DEFINE MATERIAL START
ISOTROPIC STEEL
E 200
POISSON 0.3
DENSITY 7.68195e-08
ALPHA 1.2e-05
DAMP 0.03
TYPE STEEL
STRENGTH FY 0.345 FU 0.448 RY 1.5 RT 1.2
ISOTROPIC CONCRETE
E 21.7185
POISSON 0.17
DENSITY 2.35616e-08
ALPHA 1e-05
DAMP 0.05
TYPE CONCRETE
STRENGTH FCU 0.0275793
END DEFINE MATERIAL
CONSTANTS
MATERIAL STEEL ALL
BETA 90 MEMB 3
* table sections, and a prismatic strut in centimetres
UNIT INCHES KIP
MEMBER PROPERTY AMERICAN
1 TO 4 TABLE ST W10X49
5 6 7 11 TABLE ST W16X26
8 9 TABLE ST W12X26
UNIT CM KN
MEMBER PROPERTY AMERICAN
10 PRIS AX 600 IX 30000 IY 20000 IZ 45000 YD 30 ZD 20
* the plate's thickness, an offset across a beam and a spring release, in inches
UNIT INCHES KIP
ELEMENT PROPERTY
101 THICKNESS 6
MEMBER OFFSET
8 START 0 -6 0
8 END 0 -6 0
MEMBER RELEASE
9 START KMZ 50000
* supports: springs in kN and m
UNIT METER KN
SUPPORTS
1 ENFORCED
4 FIXED
7 PINNED
8 FIXED BUT MY KMX 2000 KMZ 2000
UNIT FEET KIP
LOAD 1 LOADTYPE Dead  TITLE DEAD
SELFWEIGHT Y -1
UNIT INCHES KIP
MEMBER LOAD
5 6 UNI GY -0.05
11 TRAP GY -0.02 -0.04 12 96
UNIT METER KN
LOAD 2 LOADTYPE Live  TITLE LIVE
MEMBER LOAD
7 UNI GY -10
5 CON GY -20 1.5
8 CMOM GZ 5 2
UNIT FEET KIP
LOAD 3 LOADTYPE Wind  TITLE WIND X
JOINT LOAD
2 5 FX 3
3 MZ 10
UNIT INCHES KIP
LOAD 4 LOADTYPE None  TITLE SETTLEMENT
SUPPORT DISPLACEMENT LOAD
1 FY -0.25
LOAD 5 LOADTYPE None  TITLE D PLUS L
REPEAT LOAD
1 1.0 2 1.0
LOAD COMBINATION 101 1.4D
1 1.4
LOAD COMBINATION 102 1.2D + 1.6L
1 1.2 2 1.6
LOAD COMBINATION 103 1.2D + 1.0L + 1.0WX
1 1.2 2 1.0 3 1.0
LOAD COMBINATION 201 D + L
1 1.0 2 1.0
LOAD COMBINATION 202 D + 0.6WX + SETTLEMENT
1 1.0 3 0.6 4 1.0
* the analysis runs in kN and m: the first print after it is in those units
UNIT METER KN
PERFORM ANALYSIS PRINT STATICS CHECK
* the envelopes, after the analysis (the first run refused them after the
* loads, the editor before them); 103 is in envelopes 1 and 3: STAAD lists it
* under both and designs it as the last's TYPE (round 4; TR.40 says the last)
DEFINE ENVELOPE
101 TO 103 ENVELOPE 1 TYPE STRENGTH
201 202 ENVELOPE 2 TYPE SERVICEABILITY
103 ENVELOPE 3 TYPE CONNECTION
END DEFINE ENVELOPE
LOAD LIST 1
PRINT SUPPORT REACTIONS
* the comparison: every case, in one set of units
UNIT INCHES KIP
LOAD LIST ALL
PRINT JOINT DISPLACEMENTS
PRINT SUPPORT REACTIONS
PRINT MEMBER FORCES
* the envelopes: which loads envelope 1 holds, then strength and deflection checks under envelopes 1 and 2
LOAD LIST ENV 1
PRINT SUPPORT REACTIONS
LOAD LIST ENV 1 2
PARAMETER 1
CODE AISC UNIFIED 2016
METHOD LRFD
FYLD 50 ALL
DFF 240 MEMB 5 6 7 11
CHECK CODE ALL
* an envelope of one load
LOAD LIST ENV 3
CHECK CODE ALL
* a check per load case
LOAD LIST 101
CHECK CODE ALL
LOAD LIST 102
CHECK CODE ALL
LOAD LIST 103
CHECK CODE ALL
FINISH
